\chapter{Test organization and reproducible reports}
\label{ch:70}
\index{Test organization and reproducible reports}

CTest orchestrates compiler, runtime, standard-library, SDK and backend profiles when built with testing enabled. Python drivers exercise actual executables, while C and C++ tests can interrogate internal APIs or forge bad intermediate structures. Optional facilities may have skips or separate providers. Document which tests ran, which skipped, and how configurations differ before comparing totals.

\section{Build a minimal regression matrix}
For a language feature, create a positive source example, a negative type case, an execution oracle and, when a checked representation is exposed, an invalid-IR fixture. Test generated and fallback scanners where tokenization is relevant. Cover an optional backend separately with its own target and runtime. Include a relocation test for packaging changes and a sanitizer configuration for lifetimes. Record failures from untouched kernel-inventory checks as their own results. Avoid aggregating past results over incompatible trees or provider revisions as if they were one green run.

\section{Place a failing observation in the right test}
Suppose a numeric example ought to print 42 followed by a newline and
exit successfully. The native harness writes the program, invokes
\OnxCodeTerm{--emit-c}, then compiles the result with the runtime and
strict C11 warnings. Only after both commands return successfully does
it run the executable and compare stdout. A missing final newline can
therefore fail a test whose source passed semantic checking and whose
generated C passed the native compiler. Preserve the captured stdout and
status; rerunning the checker alone cannot settle a disagreement about
the bytes written by a running program.

Change the experiment to a JSON-owner cleanup regression. A counting fixture
can make one extra release visible, but its result is about the generated
sequence of calls against that fixture. The real JSON integration test
links the canonical kernel; if its required parent headers are absent,
status 77 is a CTest skip. Reporting both as successful JSON integration
would turn a missing input into an apparent measurement. Conversely, a
failure in the counting fixture can be useful even before a real kernel
checkout is available.

When reporting a sanitizer result, identify which executable was
instrumented. A sanitizer-enabled compiler can diagnose its own allocation
error while emitting perfectly ordinary C. To observe an invalid access
in the emitted program, the native test compilation and link need the
sanitizer flags too. The additional flags in the harness are separate
argument values, so preserve their boundaries in the report. Reproducing
the native link is especially important when a test includes an allocator
fixture in addition to the normal runtime.

